WEBVTT

00:24:28.246 --> 00:24:30.579
This is like a really sad thing
for human creativity.

00:24:30.579 --> 00:24:33.913
Like, you know, why are you doing this?
This is like whatever.

00:24:34.454 --> 00:24:37.538
And he was so excited. And he's like,
this has been so inspiring.

00:24:37.579 --> 00:24:39.038
I want to do a new album with this.

00:24:39.371 --> 00:24:41.038
You know, it's like, give
me all these new ideas.

00:24:41.038 --> 00:24:42.704
It's making me much better at my job.

00:24:42.704 --> 00:24:44.829
I'm going to make better music
because of this tool.

00:24:45.371 --> 00:24:48.163
And that was awesome. And I hope that's
how it all continues to go.

00:24:48.579 --> 00:24:50.204
And I think it is going to lead to this.

00:24:50.371 --> 00:24:51.913
We see a similar thing now with Dolly,

00:24:52.121 --> 00:24:56.121
where graphic designers sometimes tell us
that they just they see this new set

00:24:56.121 --> 00:24:58.746
of possibilities because there's
new creative inspiration

